{
  "description": "Renames of public terms. scripts/rename-terms.mjs applies the rules in order; scripts/check-terms.mjs fails on every retired pattern. To rename a term again, append rules that turn the current name into the new one, add the current name to retired, and run the script. The `api` stage renames only identifiers and event names and is safe in any repository; the `term` stage also renames the word in prose and code, so a repository that uses the word in another sense takes only `api` (with --paths to leave its records of past work alone) and edits its own text by hand. The word `dataset` is also the DOM property `element.dataset`: protect `.dataset.` except in `draw.dataset.` before renaming it again. The changelogs record the names of their versions, and check-terms.mjs reads them too: a retired name a changelog keeps between backticks is retired everywhere but between backticks.",
